  "rules": {
    "title": "How to play",
    "body": "The goal is to **capture more of the opponent's pieces** than they capture of yours.\n**First turn**: a coin decides the order. Side I — the player who created the game goes first; II — the other one does.\n**Phase 1 — draft**: take turns blindly drawing a piece and placing it on any free square, 4 per side.\n**Phase 2 — moves**: each piece may move **only once** the whole game, sliding along its own directions up to its **range** (select a piece to see its arrows).\n**Piece markings**: the pill shows **range** as a number and a **direction icon** (legend before the table).\n**Archers** (Orc Archer, Shelob, Wizard, Elven Warrior) **slide to empty squares** like other pieces; if an **enemy** is **first** on a ray, they **shoot from place** (without entering that square). **Dashed** arrows mark shots and ↗ on the badge; in the table — • in the **Archer** column.\nYou capture by moving onto an enemy piece. There are two cases:\n• **Clean capture** — if that piece can't strike your attacker back, you take it automatically.\n• **Duel** — if the defending piece also threatens the attacker, a coin decides: side I captures, II misses. On a miss the attacking piece stays put and its move is spent.\nWhen no moves remain, whoever **captured more pieces** wins; an equal count is a **draw**.",
